## Why 3ct Marquise Lab Beats 3ct Round Lab on Size Per Dollar

A 3ct round lab diamond measures 9.3 mm across — face-up area of 67.9 mm². A 3ct marquise lab measures 15.0 × 7.5 mm — face-up area of 88.4 mm². The marquise beats the round on area by 30%, on length by 61%, and on starting lab price by 15% ($3,819 vs $4,500 typical).

For buyers who want the biggest-looking lab stone per dollar at the 3ct tier, marquise is the clear winner on face-up measurements. The one trade-off is the Width Floor — a 3ct marquise is 7.5 mm wide vs 9.3 mm for the round, so side-to-side finger coverage lags.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Spec</th><th>3ct Marquise Lab</th><th>3ct Round Lab</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Face-up (mm)</strong></td><td>15.0 × 7.5</td><td>9.3 Ø</td><td>Marquise is 61% longer than round diameter.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Face-up area (mm²)</strong></td><td>88.4</td><td>67.9</td><td>Marquise wins area by 30%.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Lab floor price</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30343375?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,819</a></td><td>~$4,500</td><td>Marquise is 15% cheaper than round at lab floor.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Reads as</strong></td><td>"Dramatic statement ring"</td><td>"Classic 3ct round"</td><td>Marquise reads bigger and more distinctive.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** For "biggest-looking lab ring per dollar" at the 3ct tier, marquise beats round on every measure that matters. Pay less, get more face-up area, get a more distinctive silhouette. The Width Floor is the trade-off — if side-to-side width matters more, pick round. Full comparison in our [round diamond vs marquise](/round-diamond-vs-marquise) guide.

> **"For my clients who want 'a 3 carat lab ring' with max visual impact, I steer them to marquise over round. The $700 saved plus the 30% area advantage adds up to a ring that reads like $8,000+ even though the stone cost $3,819. That is the Elongation Illusion delivering its last big win on the marquise chart — above 3ct the advantage narrows."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

## How to Verify a 3 Carat Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every stone must pass before you add to cart.

**Check 1 — The certificate measurements.** For a 3ct marquise at 2.00 L:W, measurements should read close to 15.0 × 7.5 × 4.7 mm. If length is below 14.5 mm, the stone is cut deep and wasting carat weight below the girdle. More in our [marquise ideal proportions guide](/marquise-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions).

**Check 2 — The HD video for bow-tie severity.** The Bow-Tie Certainty applies at 3ct as it does at 2ct. Open the 360° HD video. Faint diagonal shading = accept. Hard dark band = reject. See [marquise diamond bow-tie](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie).

**Check 3 — Confirm the setting supports V-tip six-prong platinum.** Before committing to the stone, confirm the setting you want satisfies all 4 Prong Rules. Standard round-prong 14k gold settings fail the check. Specify platinum V-tip six-prong from the start.

I run these three checks on every 3ct marquise before I quote a client. The stone has to pass the first two. The setting choice is the third — and often the difference between a ring that lasts 50 years intact and one that comes back with a chipped tip or lost stone after 18 months.

